/* book Worked example 2: Q: A T-section spar cap has a flange 100 mm × 10 mm on top and a web 10 mm thick and 90 mm deep below it (total depth 100 mm). It carries a sagging moment of 3 kN·m (bottom fibres in tension), so Mx = −3 kN·m in this book's convention. Find the neutral axis, I, the two section moduli and the top and bottom stresses. Which face yields first?
   1. Areas: flange A₁ = 1000 mm² with centroid 5 mm below the top; web A₂ = 900 mm² with centroid 10 + 45 = 55 mm below the top.
   2. Centroid from the top: ȳ = (1000 × 5 + 900 × 55)/1900 = 28.68 mm. So ytop = 28.68 mm and ybot = 100 − 28.68 = 71.32 mm.
   3. I = [100 × 10³/12 + 1000 × (28.68 − 5)²] + [10 × 90³/12 + 900 × (55 − 28.68)²] = 569,275 + 1,230,769 = 1,800,044 mm⁴.
   4. Ztop = I/ytop = 62,754 mm³; Zbot = I/ybot = 25,240 mm³.
   5. Top fibre, y = +28.68 mm: σ = Mx y/I = (−3 × 10⁶ × 28.68)/1,800,044 = -47.8 N/mm² (compression).
   6. Bottom fibre, y = −71.32 mm: σ = (−3 × 10⁶)(−71.32)/1,800,044 = +118.9 N/mm² (tension).
   Answer: The neutral axis is 28.68 mm below the top; I = 1,800,044 mm⁴; Ztop = 62,754 mm³ and Zbot = 25,240 mm³. The top carries -47.8 MPa and the bottom +118.9 MPa, so the bottom fibre, 71.32 mm from the neutral axis, yields first. */
