/* book Worked example 2: Q: Find the same two stresses by the principal axis method.
   1. tan 2θ = −2 × 250,000/(666,667 − 166,667) = −1.000, so 2θ = −45° and θ = -22.5°.
   2. Iu, Iv = 416,667 ± √(250,000² + 250,000²) = 416,667 ± 353,553: Iu = 770,220 mm⁴, Iv = 63,113 mm⁴. Check: Iuv = 250,000 sin(−45°) + 250,000 cos(−45°) = 0.
   3. Mu = Mx cos θ = 923,880 N·mm; Mv = Mx sin θ = -382,683 N·mm.
   4. Point A (0, 50): u = 50 sin θ = -19.13 mm, v = 50 cos θ = 46.19 mm. σ = 923,880 × 46.19/770,220 + (-382,683)(-19.13)/63,113 = 55.4 + 116.0 = 171.4 MPa.
   5. Point B (50, 50): u = 27.06 mm, v = 65.33 mm. σ = 78.4 + (-164.1) = -85.7 MPa.
   Answer: The same 171.4 MPa at A and -85.7 MPa at B: the three methods are one formula seen three ways. */
